{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan","id":393585,"title":"The Jiang Shi as a Clan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-05T03:17:14-08:00","id":393585,"title":"The Jiang Shi as a Clan?","content":"While the Jiang Shi are very interesting and the source of plenty of plot material as written in Blood &amp; Smoke, their very inclusion and similarity to the other five Clans got me thinking. One of my personal theories is that the five Clans of the Kindred used to be completely separate monsters, but they began to mingle and exchanged Vitae and gradually became different faces of the same kind of creature. Much in the book seems to encourage this, even. Which makes one wonder, what if this happened to the Jiang Shi today? What would have to be removed, how do you give them a legitimate Curse and unique Discipline? The idea of a brand new Clan emerging just intrigues me and it further helps cement the mysteries of just what the vampiric condition is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Obviously the heart transplant thing would have to go. Maybe teleportation would evolve into a full Discipline? Their Curse could be tied to their sleeping ground somehow. Just take what already is there and turn it into more of a legitimate Clan as the others are written. How would you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","name":"Deraneo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T03:52:06-08:00","id":393627,"title":"","content":"You are aware of the theory that the clans aren't related at all, and the inherent similarities come from their shared origins as former humans, aren't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T05:05:49-08:00","id":393655,"title":"","content":"Kindred is a term coined by the Roman Sennex, then later stolen by the Lance. At first, it refered to the &quot;royal&quot; line of Julii, refering to how the clan Julii were all family by blood, and thus priviledged over non-Kindred vamps (all other clans). Then, the Lance was all like, &quot;we are all Kindred&quot; meaning that the clans are all equal (in God's purpose for the damned, etc).<br /> <br /> Fast forward to modern day. Now, its a term to refer to politically acceptable forms of vamps allowed in the Danse Macabre / All Night Society. Make no mistake, the Kindred (barring clueless neonates) know there are other kinds of vamps beyond the five clans. If they should be included or not in their society (and thus be considered Kindred) depends on individual cities.<br /> <br /> If you want to make them more mechanically aligned with other clans? That is harder, as there is a lot of thematic overlap with the scholastic Shadows. You would need merits, new Signature discipline that supported their book habit, and drawback.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I do with them is have them more strix-like than the average vampire. More spirit than flesh. Ergo, no physical discipline. Their signature power involves Fate weaving. Both the Owls and example Jaing-Shi in the book have a sense for disaster and misfortune. Their &quot;appear at grave&quot; clan ability is very spirit like, as if it was an anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T00:47:24-08:00","id":394579,"title":"","content":"Thing is, the Jiang Shi already are a clan. With a lot more going for them than any of the others. Making them anything else might dilute them somewhat from being what they are supposed to be. A different &quot;breed&quot; of Vampire. If one wanted to give them more flavour, perhaps stuff to represent the strange sorceries that they apparently wield, then I would recommend Devotions. If you happen to have a copy of the Wicked Dead, some inspirations for such Devotions can readily be found in the Jiang Shi section found in that book.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Jiang Shi in Wicked Dead, I actually didn't remember that section existed until I did a bit of research on the net last night regarding the Jiang Shi of myth. There was a list of references to them in pop culture, and the Wicked Dead was mentioned. So I went to take a peek, and found that even though they are less Kindred, and more a weird sort of Revenant type thing, there were still some similarities between them and the clan. So it was pretty clear those same Jiang Shi were part of the inspiration for how they turned out in Blood and Smoke.<br /> <br /> The Mask of a Thousand Faces power they have could easily be seen as Obfuscate 4, and the power was named such back in the days of Masquerade. The return to grave thing is already covered. Dust on the Wind could be an interesting Celerity and Obfuscate Devotion. The weird demon bird thing sounds a bit too close to Protean for my liking, but heck, maybe it could be an Animalism 2 Devotion which only works on birds of prey, or carrion birds, where the Jiang Shi possesses a corpse of such a creature and mutates it into a horrid demon birdy. Probably keep the claws and talons from doing aggy, though.<br /> <br /> Maybe create a few new ones too, mixing and matching their 3 disciplines as you see fit. And maybe give one or two of them a more ritualistic feel to them, which is something I find works well for ones with Animalism as their base. Probably best not go much more than 5 devotions total, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T11:14:08-08:00","id":396541,"title":"","content":"The weakness should be altered. A vampire who goes into frenzy every time someone lights a cigar or makes some impolite remark in the same room isn\u00b4t likely to have much of a social life with either kindred or mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:25:08-07:00","id":444708,"title":"","content":"As a bit of trivia: originally the Jiang Shi, Ghuul and Cihuateteo were written together in a single chapter in Wicked Dead. The idea was that they were different cultural takes on the same phenomenon, an idea that got lost in the final printed product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4030-alexs","name":"AlexS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:57:59-07:00","id":444805,"title":"","content":"Umm... Has no one here read The Triangle writeup in VtR 2e? It literally has a Kindred clan version of Jiang Shi...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:37:53-07:00","id":445429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan?p=444805#post444805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Has no one here read The Triangle writeup in VtR 2e? It literally has a Kindred clan version of Jiang Shi...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That I have. And my rant on post 4 was supposed to help folks expand on what was already written, but I think folks might have missed that. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:55:08-07:00","id":445439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlexS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan?p=444708#post444708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a bit of trivia: originally the Jiang Shi, Ghuul and Cihuateteo were written together in a single chapter in Wicked Dead. The idea was that they were different cultural takes on the same phenomenon, an idea that got lost in the final printed product.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely an interesting bit of trivia, Mister Scokel! Was there a particular root phenomenon described, or was it a more general thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:31:20-07:00","id":446679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan?p=445439#post445439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's definitely an interesting bit of trivia, Mister Scokel! Was there a particular root phenomenon described, or was it a more general thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been a while, and obviously it underwent some revision before being printed, but I believe the focus was on ways mortals might interact with the force behind the blood to become things that were like the Kindred, and how those might give rise to regional vampire myths. I think I was playing off of the idea of vampires of different clans being similar but separate creatures, and how such might come to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4030-alexs","name":"AlexS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T04:42:22-07:00","id":449005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlexS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan?p=446679#post446679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's been a while, and obviously it underwent some revision before being printed, but I believe the focus was on ways mortals might interact with the force behind the blood to become things that were like the Kindred, and how those might give rise to regional vampire myths. I think I was playing off of the idea of vampires of different clans being similar but separate creatures, and how such might come to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, i think the &quot;discipline sets&quot; suggested for Ghuls and Cihuateteo both in Wicked Dead are pretty close to the Daeva package. Would have to check out to be 100% sure, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:25:16-07:00","id":449101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan?p=444805#post444805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Has no one here read The Triangle writeup in VtR 2e? It literally has a Kindred clan version of Jiang Shi...</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. I took that into account when I said my piece too. I was operating under the assumption that the OP wanted to take that bare-bones write up a step further. Flesh it out more. I did for my personal use. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T07:58:56-07:00","id":449273,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, my misunderstanding then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T21:49:22-07:00","id":455399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deraneo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/393585-the-jiang-shi-as-a-clan#post393585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously the heart transplant thing would have to go. Maybe teleportation would evolve into a full Discipline? Their Curse could be tied to their sleeping ground somehow. Just take what already is there and turn it into more of a legitimate Clan as the others are written. How would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? It's just a more elaborate and gory embrace when one stops to think hard about it. Make the transplant between sire &amp; child and you're set to go...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}